Adds a self-learning correction system that detects when the user repeats
a misheard command and learns the correction automatically. Zero RAM cost.

Rust side (stt_learning.rs — new file):
- SttLearningState: tracks pending failures + learned corrections
- log_failed_transcript: called when parser can't handle STT output
- log_successful_transcript: compares with recent failure, learns diff
- get_learned_corrections: returns auto-apply corrections to frontend
- Storage: %APPDATA%/com.nexus.assistant/learned_corrections.json
- Learning rules:
  * Only learn when 1-2 words differ at same positions
  * Require 3 consistent corrections before auto-applying
  * Only learn within 30-second window (user repeated quickly)
  * Skip words < 3 chars or Levenshtein distance > 3
  * Context-aware: stores word-before for position-specific corrections
- 11 unit tests (word_diff, levenshtein, edge cases)

Frontend side (recorder.ts):
- loadLearnedCorrections(): loads auto-apply corrections at startup
- logFailedTranscript/logSuccessfulTranscript: IPC calls to Rust
- correctSttTranscript(): applies learned corrections after hardcoded ones
- Both capture paths (finishCapture + finishCaptureFromVad) log
  failures and successes

Tests: 104 Rust tests pass (93 existing + 11 new), 10 offline command
tests pass, 808 frontend modules build.

RAM cost: ~1-10 KB (in-memory HashMap + JSON file)

